        "description": "<figure>\n\n<img alt=\"Some Horizon Worlds avatars hanging out around a virtual campfire.\" data-caption=\"\" data-portal-copyright=\"Image: Meta\" data-has-syndication-rights=\"1\" src=\"https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/chorus/uploads/chorus_asset/file/24396993/328431170_528558606050894_138216244473781208_n.png?quality=90&#038;strip=all&#038;crop=0,0,100,100\" />\n\t<figcaption>\n\t\t</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p class=\"has-text-align-none\">Meta is reversing its plans to shut down its VR metaverse - sort of.</p>\n<p class=\"has-text-align-none\">On Monday, the company announced that it would be shutting down the VR version of its 3D social platform Horizon Worlds <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/896322/meta-is-shutting-down-its-vr-metaverse-on-june-15th\">on June 15th</a> in favor of a <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/881647/meta-vr-mobile-metaverse-horizon-worlds\">new focus on the mobile version of the app</a>. But in a Wednesday AMA on his Instagram, Meta CTO Andrew Bos",
